#: ../../../readme.md:73
msgid "Basic Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:74
msgid "In the Browser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:76
msgid ""
"The bare minimum for using highlight.js on a web page is linking to the "
"library along with one of the themes and calling [`highlightAll`][1]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:79
msgid ""
"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/path/to/styles/default.min.css\">\n"
"<script src=\"/path/to/highlight.min.js\"></script>\n"
"<script>hljs.highlightAll();</script>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:85
msgid ""
"This will find and highlight code inside of `<pre><code>` tags; it tries to "
"detect the language automatically. If automatic detection doesn’t work for "
"you, or you simply prefer to be explicit, you can specify the language "
"manually by using the `class` attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:90
msgid "<pre><code class=\"language-html\">...</code></pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:94
msgid "Plaintext Code Blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:96
msgid ""
"To apply the Highlight.js styling to plaintext without actually highlighting "
"it, use the `plaintext` language:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:98
msgid "<pre><code class=\"language-plaintext\">...</code></pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:102
msgid "Ignoring a Code Block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:104
msgid ""
"To skip highlighting of a code block completely, use the `nohighlight` class:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:106
msgid "<pre><code class=\"nohighlight\">...</code></pre>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:110
msgid "Node.js on the Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:112
msgid "The bare minimum to auto-detect the language and highlight some code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:114
msgid ""
"// load the library and ALL languages\n"
"hljs = require('highlight.js');\n"
"html = hljs.highlightAuto('<h1>Hello World!</h1>').value\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:120
msgid "To load only a \"common\" subset of popular languages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:122
msgid "hljs = require('highlight.js/lib/common');\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:126
msgid "To highlight code with a specific language, use `highlight`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:128
msgid ""
"html = hljs.highlight('<h1>Hello World!</h1>', {language: 'xml'}).value\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:132
msgid ""
"See [Importing the Library](#importing-the-library) for more examples of "
"`require` vs `import` usage, etc.  For more information about the result "
"object returned by `highlight` or `highlightAuto` refer to the [api docs]"
"(https://highlightjs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:136
msgid "Supported Languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:138
msgid ""
"Highlight.js supports over 180 languages in the core library.  There are "
"also 3rd party language definitions available to support even more "
"languages. You can find the full list of supported languages in "
"[SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES.md][9]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:141
msgid "Custom Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:143
msgid ""
"If you need a bit more control over the initialization of Highlight.js, you "
"can use the [`highlightElement`][3] and [`configure`][4] functions. This "
"allows you to better control *what* to highlight and *when*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:147
msgid ""
"For example, here’s the rough equivalent of calling [`highlightAll`][1] but "
"doing the work manually instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:149
msgid ""
"document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', (event) => {\n"
"  document.querySelectorAll('pre code').forEach((el) => {\n"
"    hljs.highlightElement(el);\n"
"  });\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:157
msgid "Please refer to the documentation for [`configure`][4] options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:160
msgid "Using custom HTML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:162
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend `<pre><code>` wrapping for code blocks. It's quite "
"semantic and \"just works\" out of the box with zero fiddling. It is "
"possible to use other HTML elements (or combos), but you may need to pay "
"special attention to preserving linebreaks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:167
msgid "Let's say your markup for code blocks uses divs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:169
msgid "<div class='code'>...</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:173
msgid "To highlight such blocks manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:175
msgid ""
"// first, find all the div.code blocks\n"
"document.querySelectorAll('div.code').forEach(el => {\n"
"  // then highlight each\n"
"  hljs.highlightElement(el);\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:183
msgid ""
"Without using a tag that preserves linebreaks (like `pre`) you'll need some "
"additional CSS to help preserve them.  You could also [pre and post-process "
"line breaks with a plug-in][brPlugin], but *we recommend using CSS*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:189
msgid "To preserve linebreaks inside a `div` using CSS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:191
msgid ""
"div.code {\n"
"  white-space: pre;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:198
msgid "Using with Vue.js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:200
msgid ""
"See [highlightjs/vue-plugin](https://github.com/highlightjs/vue-plugin) for "
"a simple Vue plugin that works great with Highlight.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:202
msgid "An example of `vue-plugin` in action:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:204
msgid ""
"  <div id=\"app\">\n"
"    <!-- bind to a data property named `code` -->\n"
"    <highlightjs autodetect :code=\"code\" />\n"
"    <!-- or literal code works as well -->\n"
"    <highlightjs language='javascript' code=\"var x = 5;\" />\n"
"  </div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:213
msgid "Using Web Workers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:215
msgid ""
"You can run highlighting inside a web worker to avoid freezing the browser "
"window while dealing with very big chunks of code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:218
msgid "In your main script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:220
msgid ""
"addEventListener('load', () => {\n"
"  const code = document.querySelector('#code');\n"
"  const worker = new Worker('worker.js');\n"
"  worker.onmessage = (event) => { code.innerHTML = event.data; }\n"
"  worker.postMessage(code.textContent);\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:229
msgid "In worker.js:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:231
msgid ""
"onmessage = (event) => {\n"
"  importScripts('<path>/highlight.min.js');\n"
"  const result = self.hljs.highlightAuto(event.data);\n"
"  postMessage(result.value);\n"
"};\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:239
msgid "Importing the Library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:241
msgid ""
"First, you'll likely be installing the library via `npm` or `yarn` -- see "
"[Getting the Library](#getting-the-library)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:244
msgid "Node.js CommonJS Modules / `require`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:246
msgid "Requiring the top-level library will load all languages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:248
msgid ""
"// require the highlight.js library, including all languages\n"
"const hljs = require('./highlight.js');\n"
"const highlightedCode = hljs.highlightAuto('<span>Hello World!</span>')."
"value\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:254
msgid ""
"For a smaller footprint, load our common subset of languages (the same set "
"used for our default web build)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:256
msgid "const hljs = require('highlight.js/lib/common');\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:260
msgid "For the smallest footprint, load only the languages you need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:262
msgid ""
"const hljs = require('highlight.js/lib/core');\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('xml', require('highlight.js/lib/languages/xml'));\n"
"\n"
"const highlightedCode = hljs.highlight('<span>Hello World!</span>', "
"{language: 'xml'}).value\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:270
msgid "Node.js ES6 Modules / `import`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:272
msgid "The default import will register all languages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:274
msgid "import hljs from 'highlight.js';\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:278
msgid ""
"It is more efficient to import only the library and register the languages "
"you need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:280
msgid ""
"import hljs from 'highlight.js/lib/core';\n"
"import javascript from 'highlight.js/lib/languages/javascript';\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('javascript', javascript);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:286
msgid ""
"If your build tool processes CSS imports, you can also import the theme "
"directly as a module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:288
msgid ""
"import hljs from 'highlight.js';\n"
"import 'highlight.js/styles/github.css';\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:293
msgid "Browser ES6 Modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:295
msgid ""
"*Note: For now you'll want to install `@highlightjs/cdn-assets` package "
"instead of `highlight.js`. See [Download prebuilt CDN assets](#download-"
"prebuilt-cdn-assets)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:298
msgid "To import the library and register only those languages that you need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:300
msgid ""
"import hljs from './assets/js/@highlightjs/cdn-assets/es/core.js';\n"
"import javascript from './assets/js/@highlightjs/cdn-assets/es/languages/"
"javascript.min.js';\n"
"\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('javascript', javascript);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:307
msgid "To import the library and register all languages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:309
msgid ""
"import hljs from './assets/js/@highlightjs/cdn-assets/es/highlight.js';\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:313
msgid ""
"*Note: The path to these files will vary depending on where you have "
"installed/copied them within your project or site. The above path is only an "
"example.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:316
msgid ""
"You can also use [`importmap`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/"
"HTML/Element/script/type/importmap) to import in similar way as Node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:318
msgid ""
"<script type=\"importmap\">\n"
"{\n"
"\t\"imports\": {\n"
"\t\t\"@highlightjs\": \"./assets/js/@highlightjs/cdn-assets/es/\"\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"</script>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:328
msgid ""
"Use the above code in your HTML. After that, your JavaScript can import "
"using the named key from your `importmap`, for example `@highlightjs` in "
"this case:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:331
msgid ""
"import hljs from '@highlightjs/core.js';\n"
"import javascript from '@highlightjs/languages/javascript.min.js';\n"
"\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('javascript', javascript);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:338
msgid ""
"*Note: You can also import directly from fully static URLs, such as our very "
"own pre-built ES6 Module CDN resources. See [Fetch via CDN](#fetch-via-cdn) "
"for specific examples.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:341
msgid "Getting the Library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:343
msgid ""
"You can get highlight.js as a hosted, or custom-build, browser script or as "
"a server module. Right out of the box the browser script supports both AMD "
"and CommonJS, so if you wish you can use RequireJS or Browserify without "
"having to build from source. The server module also works perfectly fine "
"with Browserify, but there is the option to use a build specific to browsers "
"rather than something meant for a server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:351
msgid ""
"**Do not link to GitHub directly.** The library is not supposed to work "
"straight from the source, it requires building. If none of the pre-packaged "
"options work for you refer to the [building documentation][6]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:355
msgid ""
"**On Almond.** You need to use the optimizer to give the module a name. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:358
msgid "r.js -o name=hljs paths.hljs=/path/to/highlight out=highlight.js\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:362
msgid "Fetch via CDN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:364
msgid ""
"A prebuilt version of Highlight.js bundled with many common languages is "
"hosted by several popular CDNs. When using Highlight.js via CDN you can use "
"Subresource Integrity for additional security.  For details see [DIGESTS.md]"
"(https://github.com/highlightjs/cdn-release/blob/main/DIGESTS.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:368
msgid "cdnjs ([link](https://cdnjs.com/libraries/highlight.js))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:370 ../../../readme.md:395 ../../../readme.md:418
msgid "Common JS <!-- omit in toc -->"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:372
msgid ""
"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/"
"highlight.js/11.11.1/styles/default.min.css\">\n"
"<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.11.1/"
"highlight.min.js\"></script>\n"
"<!-- and it's easy to individually load additional languages -->\n"
"<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.11.1/"
"languages/go.min.js\"></script>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:379 ../../../readme.md:404 ../../../readme.md:427
msgid "ES6 Modules <!-- omit in toc -->"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:381
msgid ""
"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/"
"highlight.js/11.11.1/styles/dark.min.css\">\n"
"<script type=\"module\">\n"
"import hljs from 'https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight."
"js/11.11.1/es/highlight.min.js';\n"
"//  and it's easy to individually load additional languages\n"
"import go from 'https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.11.1/"
"es/languages/go.min.js';\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('go', go);\n"
"</script>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:393
msgid ""
"jsdelivr ([link](https://www.jsdelivr.com/package/gh/highlightjs/cdn-"
"release))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:397
msgid ""
"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-"
"release@11.11.1/build/styles/default.min.css\">\n"
"<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-release@11.11.1/"
"build/highlight.min.js\"></script>\n"
"<!-- and it's easy to individually load additional languages -->\n"
"<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-release@11.11.1/"
"build/languages/go.min.js\"></script>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../readme.md:406
msgid ""
"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-"
"release@11.11.1/build/styles/default.min.css\">\n"
"<script type=\"module\">\n"
"import hljs from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-"
"release@11.11.1/build/es/highlight.min.js';\n"
"//  and it's easy to individually load additional languages\n"
"import go from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/highlightjs/cdn-release@11.11.1/"
"build/es/languages/go.min.js';\n"
"hljs.registerLanguage('go', go);\n"
"</script>\n"
msgstr ""

